---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAPPING (web → native; values verified by the executed swift test below)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  shell:  <FadeIn><GlassPanel className="p-4"> … </GlassPanel></FadeIn>
            → TSFadeIn { TSGlassPanel { VStack { freshnessHeader? ; content } } }
              (web FadeIn → TSFadeIn; web GlassPanel → TSGlassPanel, whose built-in
              TSSpacing.lg padding is the p-4 parity). The freshness chip is
              native-only chrome inside the panel.
  row:    <div className="flex items-center justify-between text-xs">
            start | duration | end → HStack { startMarker; Spacer; duration;
            Spacer; endMarker } (justify-between parity: start leading, duration
            centered, end trailing) at Font.TS.caption (web text-xs = 12px).
  start:  <span className="text-green-400"><Flag/>{formatTime(drive.startTs)}</span>
            → DriveTimelineMarker(.start): flag.fill (Color.TS.statusSuccess) +
              startTimeText. formatTime → jjmm (locale 12/24h), nil/invalid → "—".
  duration:<span className="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
            {formatDuration(drive.durationS / 60)}</span>
            → Text(durationText) in Color.TS.textMuted. duration() is a VERBATIM
              port of helpers.ts formatDuration applied to durationS/60:
              h = floor(min/60); m = round(min%60); h>0 ? "Hh Mm" : "Mm".
  end:    <span className="text-red-400"><Flag/>{drive.endTs ?
            formatTime(drive.endTs) : t('driveDetail.inProgress','In progress')}</span>
            → DriveTimelineMarker(.end): flag.fill (Color.TS.statusDanger) +
              endLabel. endLabel = formatTime(endTs) when finished, else the
              localized "In progress" (web `drive.endTs ? … : t(…)`).
  bar:    <div className="h-3 rounded-full bg-[var(--surface-2)]">
            <div className="h-full w-full bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-500
            to-cyan-400"/></div>
            → DriveTimelineProgressTrack: a 12pt Capsule track (Color.TS.surface +
              border) with a full-width LinearGradient capsule
              [Color.TS.statusSuccess → Color.TS.accent] (emerald→cyan on-token,
              NOT a Tailwind port). The web renders a STATIC 100%-width gradient
              (no computed percentage), so the native bar mirrors that exactly
              (Covenant #5/#9 — no drift to a fake progress value).
  i18n:   driveDetail.inProgress (web-source parity) + native chrome
            (driveTimeline.{live,stale,offline,updating,loading,unavailable,
            errorTitle,retry,startLabel,durationLabel,endLabel}), table
            "DriveTimeline". 12 keys, full bidirectional coverage.

STATES (every one renders — verified by the ImageRenderer tests [6]):
  loading → DriveTimelineSkeleton (skeleton start/duration/end row + skeleton bar;
            Reduce-Motion safe via TSSkeleton).
  content → DriveTimelineBar (start + duration + end + gradient bar). Two flavours:
            finished drive (end shows formatTime(endTs)) and in-progress (end shows
            the localized "In progress").
  empty   → DriveTimelineEmpty (no drive resolved): a friendly
            "Drive timeline unavailable" caption above a faint, unfilled track —
            never a blank box.
  error   → DriveTimelineErrorView (web QueryError): danger glyph + "Couldn't load
            drive timeline" + message + Retry → model.refresh().
  stale   → freshness chip (Stale) + ONE guarded auto-refresh; cached bar stays.
  offline → freshness chip (Offline); cached bar stays, no refetch.
a11y: the start/duration/end row is one combined element with a spoken summary
  (DriveTimelineAccessibility.summary = "Start <t>, Duration <d>, End <t|In
  progress>"); the gradient bar + decorative flag glyphs are accessibilityHidden;
  Reduce-Motion fill gate (TSFadeIn); Dynamic Type via tokens/system fonts.
telemetry: P1/S11 view.opened(surface:"DriveTimeline") emitted exactly once on
  appear (asserted by testStartEmitsViewOpenedOnce).
binding: P1/S8 DriveTimelineSource seam (production impl over the shared
  DrivingStore + SettingsStore for the locale/zone); the view performs NO
  networking. Previews/tests use InMemoryDriveTimelineSource.

